        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 86-year-old female patient, admitted on 15/03/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency, and blood tests showing elevated inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout her stay. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. She was discharged on 16/03/2022 with optimised inhaler therapy and oral corticosteroids. We recommend close outpatient follow-up and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
